{
  "description": "Minor Material Amendment to application Ref: 26/AP/2437 dated 15/10/2026 for Erection of single-storey seperate rear extensions to both properties following demolition of the existing single-storey rear outriggers, construction of detached garden studios, associated hard and soft landscaping works, and removal of existing rooflights with the installation of replacement and additional rooflights within the existing loft spaces.\rThe proposed variation seeks to incorporate an air source heat pump (ASHP) and air conditioning system to improve the dwelling's operational energy performance and resilience to future climate conditions.\rThe ASHP would provide an efficient, electrically powered solution for space heating and domestic hot water, reducing reliance on fossil fuels and supporting a reduction in operational carbon emissions.\rThe proposed air conditioning system would provide additional protection against overheating, helping to future-proof the dwelling in response to climate change and the increasing frequency, duration and intensity of periods of high summer temperatures.\rTogether, these measures aim to improve the long-term energy performance, thermal comfort and climate resilience of the dwelling.\rTo vary the approved design proposal to include an ASHP and Air Con unit within the front gardens for both 384 and 386 Lordship Lane.\r\r\r\r\r\r",
